From 0729102f128bba8bcdabbe4d2b2ed328c470c314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:14:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/56] Blades dashboard (2.0.2858): fixes found by walking
 every blade

- Threads: a new thread without an explicit processor reports its parent's
  hardware thread (XDK: children stay on the parent's thread until
  XSetThreadProcessor), and a title's main thread starts on hardware thread
  0. The dashboard treats a nonzero previous processor from
  XSetThreadProcessor as failure and abandoned its Pictures screen. Host
  threads still spread over cores.
- XMPGetMediaSources: succeed with no sources (none emulated) instead of
  E_INVALIDARG (Pictures).
- XConfig: media center category (never paired: zeroed, Computers screen),
  composite screen size, and a value buffer large enough for the 0x40-byte
  settings.
- VdGetDisplayDiscoveryData (no HDMI on these consoles: FALSE) and
  VdEnumerateVideoModes (no modes) instead of undefined imports, which made
  the Display pane show a time zone as the video mode.
- DVD drive: XN_SYS_TRAYSTATECHANGED carries the media state (0 none,
  1 360 game, 3 unknown, 4 DVD, ... as the dashboard's disc tile shows it),
  XamLoaderGetDvdTrayState answers 0 closed / 2 open and
  HalOpenCloseODDTray(1) opens: an empty drive is now "Open Tray"/"Close
  Tray" instead of "Unrecognized Disc". A console powers on with the tray
  closed.
- Research: the patched-module dump also writes the running dashboard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AFb8CDFE1Ms5NnJH88eG8b
